61:\title{Cycle tilings and $H$-factors in directed graphs}
82:We prove several results concerning cycle tilings and $H$-factors in digraphs.
84:In addition, we asymptotically determine the minimum degree threshold for forcing an $H$-factor in a digraph for a range of digraphs $H$, including the cases when $H$ is a tree or anti-directed cycle. Furthermore, 
85: an asymptotically exact Ore-type result for forcing a transitive tournament factor in a digraph is  proven. Several related open problems are also highlighted.
94:\section{Introduction}
95:\subsection{Minimum degree conditions forcing $H$-factors}
96:The focus of this paper is on cycle tilings and  $H$-factors in digraphs. Unless stated otherwise, the digraphs we consider do not have loops and we allow for at most one edge in each direction between any pair of vertices.
