Let $C_t$ denote the directed cycle on $t$ vertices; so $C_3$ is the cyclic triangle. In the \textit{(undirected) graph} setting, we will also write $C_t$ for the cycle on $t$ vertices.
Building on a number of earlier results,  K\"uhn and Osthus~\cite{KuhnO} determined, up to an additive constant, the minimum degree threshold for forcing a  $H$-factor in a graph $G$, for \textit{any} fixed graph $H$. We now state their result in the case of cycle factors.
Given $k \in \mathbb N$ we define $\chi^* (C_{2k}):=2$ and $\chi^* (C_{2k+1}):=1+1/k$. 
\begin{theorem}\label{kocycle} \cite{KuhnO}
    Given any $t \geq 3$, there exists a constant $C=C(t) $
    such that the following holds.  If  $G$ is a graph whose order $n$ is divisible by $|H|$ and  
$$\delta (G)  \geq \left (1 - \frac{1}{\chi^* (H)} \right )n + C,$$ 
then $G$ contains a $C_t$-factor. Moreover, the condition on $\delta(G)$ is tight up to the value of  $C$.
\end{theorem}


