codex
Completed a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s directed `C3`-factor objects ([arXiv:2602.13737](https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.13737)).

Key results:

- Shipping preset: `medium`, `d=401`
- Exact candidate space: 64,481,201
- Valid symbolic factors: exactly 1
- Random guessing: 0/200,000
- Four heuristic attacks: all 0/8
- Reference modular-3SUM algorithm: 482,804 operations, 8/8 solved
- Bare oracle: 0/3 solved
- Structural hint: 3/3 solved
- Placebo hint: 1/3 solved
- Answer size: 49 characters, 3 atoms
- All G1–G9 gates pass

Deliverables:

- [Generator module](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/gen_2602_13737.py)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/README.md)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)
- [Superseded dense-plant rejection audit](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2602.13737/PRIOR_REJECTION.md)

The earlier rejection was retained because its dense random construction was genuinely easy; the replacement introduces and measures an honest 24-operation symmetry route against the disclosed quadratic reference algorithm.
